%description:

Building penetration loss of Tr38901PathLossModel for an indoor UE in the UMa
and RMa scenarios, checked against section 7.4.3 and Tables 7.4.3-1 to 7.4.3-3
of 3GPP TR 38.901 v16.1.0.

The O2I loss PL_tw + PL_in is added to the outdoor path loss, so it is
measured here as the difference between the indoor and the outdoor result of
computePathLoss() with otherwise identical parameters. Every case therefore
computes its own result and states the arguments its reference formula is to
be evaluated at.

For UMa below 6 GHz Table 7.4.3-3 applies, the single-frequency model kept for
backwards compatibility with TR 36.873: the through-wall term is a constant
20 dB whose sigma_P is 0, so the whole O2I loss is deterministic. Above 6 GHz
Table 7.4.3-2 applies, a frequency-dependent median plus sigma_P times a
standard-normal variate. The variate is the UE's, drawn once (TR 38.901
7.4.3.1: "UT-specifically generated") and given to the model, so each case is
exact: the median at a deviate of 0, and the median plus sigma_P at 1.

Which of the two tables applies is a function of the scenario as well as the
frequency: only UMa and UMi are offered the sub-6 GHz model, and RMa keeps the
low-loss variant of table 7.4.3-2 at every frequency. TR 38.901 defines no O2I
loss for the indoor-office scenario at all, so what the model adds there is not
checked -- there is no expected value to derive.

Each case names the formula of pathloss_reference.py it is to be graded
against; the formulas themselves are quoted there.

%includes:
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/channelmodel/Tr38901PathLossModel.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
CaseRecorder probe(this, 1e-6);
Tr38901PathLossModel m;
ScenarioParams outdoor, indoor;

// --- fc <= 6 GHz: the deterministic model of table 7.4.3-3 ------------
outdoor = ScenarioParams();
outdoor.scenario = URBAN_MACROCELL;
outdoor.hNodeB = 25;
outdoor.hUe = 1.5;
outdoor.carrierFrequencyGHz = 2.0;

outdoor.apply(m, this);
double umaLos = m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, true);
double umaNlos = m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, false);

indoor = outdoor;
indoor.insideBuilding = true;

indoor.insideDistance = 10;
indoor.apply(m, this);
probe.record("t901_o2i_sub6", indoor, { { "dIn", 10 } },
        m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, true) - umaLos);
probe.record("t901_o2i_sub6", indoor, { { "dIn", 10 } },
        m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, false) - umaNlos);

indoor.insideDistance = 25;
indoor.apply(m, this);
probe.record("t901_o2i_sub6", indoor, { { "dIn", 25 } },
        m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, true) - umaLos);

// The indoor distance cannot exceed the length of the link, so a 50 m indoor
// leg of a 20 m link is graded as the 20 m one it is clamped to.
outdoor.apply(m, this);
double umaShort = m.computePathLoss(20, 18, true);
indoor.insideDistance = 50;
indoor.apply(m, this);
probe.record("t901_o2i_sub6", indoor, { { "dIn", 20 } },
        m.computePathLoss(20, 18, true) - umaShort);

// --- fc > 6 GHz: the material-based model of table 7.4.3-2 ------------
// Its through-wall term is sigma_P times the UE's standard-normal deviate.

outdoor = ScenarioParams();
outdoor.scenario = URBAN_MACROCELL;
outdoor.hNodeB = 25;
outdoor.hUe = 1.5;
outdoor.carrierFrequencyGHz = 28.0;
outdoor.apply(m, this);
double mmWaveOutdoor = m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, true);

indoor = outdoor;
indoor.insideBuilding = true;
indoor.insideDistance = 10;

for (double z : { 0.0, 1.0 }) {
    indoor.penetrationDeviate = z;
    indoor.apply(m, this);
    m.setUseBuildingPenetrationHighLossModel(false);
    probe.record("t901_o2i_lowloss", indoor, { { "dIn", 10 }, { "z", z } },
            m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, true) - mmWaveOutdoor);

    indoor.apply(m, this);
    m.setUseBuildingPenetrationHighLossModel(true);
    probe.record("t901_o2i_highloss", indoor, { { "dIn", 10 }, { "z", z } },
            m.computePathLoss(102.7, 100, true) - mmWaveOutdoor);
}
indoor.penetrationDeviate = 0;

// --- RMa: the low-loss model of table 7.4.3-2 at every frequency ------
outdoor = ScenarioParams();
outdoor.scenario = RURAL_MACROCELL;
outdoor.hNodeB = 35;
outdoor.hUe = 1.5;

indoor = outdoor;
indoor.insideBuilding = true;
indoor.insideDistance = 10;

outdoor.carrierFrequencyGHz = 2.0;
outdoor.apply(m, this);
double rmaOutdoor = m.computePathLoss(501.1, 500, true);

indoor.carrierFrequencyGHz = 2.0;
indoor.penetrationDeviate = 1.0;
indoor.apply(m, this);
probe.record("t901_o2i_lowloss", indoor, { { "dIn", 10 }, { "z", 1.0 } },
        m.computePathLoss(501.1, 500, true) - rmaOutdoor);

outdoor.carrierFrequencyGHz = 0.8;
outdoor.apply(m, this);
rmaOutdoor = m.computePathLoss(501.1, 500, true);

indoor.carrierFrequencyGHz = 0.8;
indoor.penetrationDeviate = -1.0;
indoor.apply(m, this);
probe.record("t901_o2i_lowloss", indoor, { { "dIn", 10 }, { "z", -1.0 } },
        m.computePathLoss(501.1, 500, true) - rmaOutdoor);

%postrun-command: ../../pathloss_reference.py --grade test.out >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=10 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
